  "description": "What never reached the backend, from the client's chair. The events on this board exist because the backend cannot report its own unreachability \u2014 they ship direct to Grafana rather than through our server for exactly that reason.\n\nBuilt from `net.*` in `docs/practices/app-events.md`. Every query here is held to the `logEvent` call sites by `DashboardQueryContractTest`.\n\n**Delivery is at-least-once.** A record can rarely ship twice (the export was acknowledged and the process died before the disk buffer's delete), so read raw counts as approximate. Panels that count *installs* or *sessions* are immune by construction \u2014 a duplicate lands in the same series and collapses.\n\n**Sampling is per session.** `telemetry.appEventsSampleRate` hashes the session id, so a sampled-out session contributes nothing at all rather than losing the middle of a funnel. Below 1.0 every absolute count here is that fraction of reality; every ratio is unaffected.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
